system "ISO:rus-Cyrl:Latn:9-1995" {

metadata {
  authority_id iso
  id 9-1995
  language iso-639-2:rus
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name "ISO 9:1995 Information and documentation -- Transliteration of Cyrillic characters into Latin characters -- Slavic and non-Slavic languages (Russian)"
  url https://www.iso.org/standard/3589.html
  creation_date 1995
  description {    Establishes a system for the transliteration into Latin characters of
    Cyrillic characters constituting the alphabets of Slavic and non-Slavic
    languages. Table 3 includes in a single sequence, listed in the
    Cyrillic alphabetic order, the 118 single or diacritic-carrying
    characters that appear in one or another of the considered alphabets.
  }
}

tests {
  # WO20 coverage audit (maps#283, 2026-11-26): exhaustive per-row tests
  # generated from the held ISO 9:1995 print (Tables 1-3). 12 map-vs-source
  # findings are recorded in the provenance artifact
  # scripts/row-sources/iso-rus-Cyrl-Latn-9-1995.json and excluded from the
  # generated tests, never forced green. Value divergences: Table 2 prints
  # ge-with-circumflex (U+011D) for ґ where the map has G-grave, and
  # y-circumflex (U+0177) for Ѵ where the map has Y-grave; Table 2 also
  # prints little-yus -> a-breve, which the map lacks entirely (its
  # a-breve value sits on big-yus, unprinted in this edition); Table 3 #3
  # prints the a-diaeresis+macron value with macron-above (U+01DF style)
  # where the map - and Table 3 #62, consistently - use dot-below
  # (U+1EA0+U+0308); #87 is the same class. Missing rules: he-with-macron
  # and dhe-with-descender (printed values partly illegible in the held
  # IHS scan). The t-variant, che/tse-variant and es-descender rows
  # (#72, 74-77, 96-101) carry diacritics illegible at available
  # magnification; the map's values there follow the official ISO 9:1995
  # repertoire and are flagged unverifiable against this print.

  "Ӧ̄ ӧ̄" -> "Ọ̈ ọ̈"
  "І̆ і̆" -> "Ĭ ĭ"
  "Ј́ ј́" -> "J́ j́"
  "У̊ у̊" -> "Ů ů"
  "ъ ь ʼ ˮ Ӏ" -> "ʺ ʹ ʼ ˮ ‡"
# Exhaustive per-row tests for iso-rus-Cyrl-Latn-9-1995, generated from the source
# document's table.
# Source: ISO 9:1995(E), clause 4 Transliteration table: Table 1 - General
# table for Slavic
# Cyrillic characters (pp. 6-9, rows 1-46), Table 2 - Complementary table
# for the Slavic
# Cyrillic characters used by some communities established outside the
# boundaries of their
# native countries (p. 10, rows 48-52), Table 3 - Table for Cyrillic
# characters of
# non-Slavic languages (p. 11, rows 1-118); held source
# interscript-private-references/iso/ISO-9-1995.pdf (IHS-licensed scan;
# watermarked).
# Extraction: the scan's OCR text layer is unusable for the character cells
# (mangled
# Cyrillic), so every row was transcribed from rendered page images
# (300-1300 dpi,
# No.-column-anchored row crops, gridline detection for Table 1; ambiguous
# cells
# re-cropped at 900-1300 dpi). Instantiation: Table 3 prints one Cyrillic
# case and one
# Latin cell per row; tests instantiate the printed cell (lowercase Cyrillic
# -> printed
# Latin; uppercase rows only where the table prints them).
# Correction table (text layer -> print): not applicable - the text layer
# carries no
# usable character cells; the No. digits alone extract reliably and served
# as row anchors.
# Findings (map-vs-source; transcribed rows EXCLUDED from the generated
# tests, never
# forced green; record for the maps-fix pipeline):
# 1. Table 2 #48: printed ґ -> gh-circumflex (gha-circumflex: U+011D); the
# map encodes
# G̀ (grave). VALUE DIVERGENCE.
# 2. Table 2 #50: printed little-yus -> a-breve (U+0103); the map has no
# little-yus rule
# at all, and its a-breve value is attached to big-yus (U+04EA -> U+01CE), a
# letter no
# printed row of this edition carries. MISSING RULE + MISATTACHED VALUE.
# 3. Table 2 #52: printed yizhitsa -> y-circumflex (U+0177); the map encodes
# Ỳ (grave,
# U+1EF2). VALUE DIVERGENCE.
# 4. Table 3 #3 (a-diaeresis+macron): the print places the macron ABOVE the
# diaeresis
# (a-diaeresis+macron, U+01DF style); the map uses dot-below + diaeresis
# (U+1EA0+U+0308).
# The print is internally inconsistent: Table 3 #62 (o-diaeresis+macron)
# prints
# dot-below (U+1EA0+U+0308 style), matching the map and the map's hand test.
# The map's
# consistent dot-below convention is retained; the print inconsistency is
# recorded.
# 5. Table 3 #87 (u-diaeresis+macron): same class as #4 - print reads as
# macron-above
# style (partially degraded); map uses dot-below + diaeresis
# (U+1EE4+U+0308). UNCERTAIN.
# 6. Table 3 #86 (ha-with-stroke): the printed Latin mark is illegible in
# the held scan
# (macron vs dot-above); the map encodes U-dot-above (U+0307). UNCERTAIN -
# flagged.
# 7. Table 3 #15: the print suggests he-with-macron (U+04FF-style) with an
# h-based value;
# the map has only the plain he rule (U+04BB -> U+1E25). MISSING
# (transcription
# uncertain).
# 8. Table 3 #25 (dhe-with-descender): printed z-with-below-mark (comma or
# dot -
# illegible); the map has no dhe-with-descender rule. MISSING.
# 9. Table 3 t-family rows 74-77 (t-with-descender variants) and che-family
# rows 96-101
# (che/tse-with-descender variants incl. diaeresis forms), plus #72
# (es-with-descender):
# the printed diacritics are illegible at any available magnification of the
# held scan.
# The map's rules for these letters (U+04AD -> U+0162, U+04B6 -> U+00C7,
# U+04B7 -> U+00C7,
# U+04BC -> U+0106, U+04BD -> U+0106, U+04BC-diaeresis -> C+combining-below
# forms,
# U+04AB -> U+015F) follow the official ISO 9:1995 repertoire but cannot be
# cell-verified against this print. UNCERTAIN - flagged for the maps-fix
# pipeline.
# 10. Table 3 #61 (barred-o + diaeresis): the printed Latin mark reads as
# diaeresis or
# double-acute at available magnification; the map encodes double-acute
# (U+0150) per
# the official repertoire. Row excluded; UNCERTAIN - flagged.
# Bookkeeping: 132 rows generated (all pass end-to-end through the ts
# runtime); the five
# map hand tests are retained; Table 1 #17/#21/#24 Latin marks (j-caron,
# l-circumflex,
# n-circumflex) were re-verified at 900 dpi against the print before
# generation; the
# excluded rows above are the complete set of printed rows not generated.
# Table 3's
# basic-letter rows duplicate Table 1's readings (the table repeats them);
# both are kept
# as printed because Table 3's rows stand on their own. Regenerating via
# scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs from this artifact reproduces the embedded block
# byte-for-byte.
# Provenance artifact: scripts/row-sources/iso-rus-Cyrl-Latn-9-1995.json (132 rows).
# generated-by: maps/scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs (2026-11-26); regenerate from the artifact, do not hand-edit.
